TY  - CHAP
AU  - El Chami, Riad
TI  - Organizational Culture and Leadership Practices Impact on the Satisfaction of the Customer
T2  - Organizational Culture in the Middle East: A Lebanese Perspective
PY  - 2022
SP  - 108
EP  - 135
PB  - Cambridge Scholars Publishing
AB  - Organizational culture is considered as a differentiation strategy that leads to long-term profits, efficiency and growth of companies. This study will focus on organizational culture. Employee motivation, employee involvement, leadership practices, and the organizational vision are considered the independent variables and customer satisfaction is considered the dependent variable for the study. The empirical part was based on a quantitative study with a questionnaire as a survey tool filled by 200 senior managers from different levels working in international companies operating in Lebanon and Dubai. The study found that Middle Eastern organizations are in need of strengthening their corporate culture to increase customer satisfaction and their retention rate.
KW  - Organizational culture
KW  - Leadership practices
KW  - Vision
KW  - Customer satisfaction
